  "body": "**Current status: draft; the frozen repair candidate passes the short performance guard, and remaining CI repairs are in progress.** The published head is still b3c7ff70 with 20 failed checks. Its hosted eight-pair results remain a recorded failure; they have not been waived or replaced by local evidence.\n\nThe [newer complete 43-path repair overlay and all 18 raw samples](https://github.com/snissn/gomap/tree/a5406f13dd05fb305c5a83d88d54686ab2cd461b/artifacts/4871/20261015-lifecycle-platform) preserve an independently verified comparison against main5bca on host111/Go1.26.3: GetVersioned +1.95% (zero allocations), DATA Batch.Write \u22123.46% (127\u2192104 allocations), and PRIMARY CommitAt +2.81% (279,177\u2192226,888 B/op; 474\u2192392 allocations). All short guards pass. This establishes bounded viability, not final acceptance or a PRIMARY speedup. Prior failed samples remain retained. [Detailed identities, boundaries and next actions](https://github.com/snissn/gomap/issues/5111#issuecomment-6193413716).\n\nFinish the remaining coherent platform, caller, retention and recovery repairs before one product push; then require current-head CI and independent review. Native integration and final Dgraph gates remain open. The implementation and historical validation below describe their explicitly named snapshots.\n\nOrdinary COW publication now keeps DATA and PRIMARY roots, their physical resources, and both recoverable capsule slots under the existing transaction and publication authority. A buffered PRIMARY update can reuse the current DATA generation; promotion shares the immutable logical root while the slot independently owns its dependency and capsule-image charge. Joint recovery and vacuum retain every actual recoverable root until its last consumer finishes.\n\nFixes #5111; part of #4871. Native pruning, original Q32/1 MiB progress and end-to-end Dgraph qualification remain separate open outcomes in #4878/#5047/#4879.\n\nCandidate: `b3c7ff702538e552e685ded554a79eb256a3380c`, tree `f847208e241240dd56e12bf5bef4c706fac3d133`, integrated with main `5bca87ffe6e1bfba2d693264d2dc82936adc234f`. This updates the existing PR by fast-forward. **Draft: qualification is in progress; not mergeable.** The first current-head formatting check failed and is being investigated with the remaining CI results before one repair batch.\n\nImplementation:\n\n- Reuse the existing COW transaction, arena, identity registry and retained-allocation owners across construction, publication, recovery, slot overwrite, vacuum and teardown. The original resource graph owns physical completion and its first failure; expired borrowed aliases cannot become second release authorities.\n- Select the existing PRIMARY format for the supported command-WAL COW backend and preserve the composite cache/backend read cut. The selected point-publication path retains the DATA generation; it does not checkpoint each foreground write.\n- Account for retained backing before effects, share original immutable slot custody, and reserve one reusable packed-cleanup handle during preparation so a retained closure can finish after DB.Close closes new admission. Real close failures retain their original handle and charge.\n- Update the storage/recovery/ownership specifications and CI input bindings. The persistent value log remains separate from the redo WAL. Pre-alpha format changes have explicit rejection/reopen coverage.\n- Keep the 275-file allocation evidence archive, including copied Go sources, on its verified [durable evidence ref](https://github.com/snissn/gomap/tree/4531e816968f89a10080164629c341d6c43e4f78/artifacts/4871/20261015-ordinary-allocation-integration), outside the product package tree. Protected power-loss testdata remains in the product.\n\nValidation so far:\n\n- Go 1.26.3 on Linux/amd64: all 344 rootpublication top-level controls passed; repaired DB producer selection had 24 passes and one explicit capability skip. The post-DB.Close failure was reproduced before the seven-file repair; all seven focused repair controls passed.\n- Exact candidate: `GOWORK=off GOTOOLCHAIN=local GOPROXY=off GOSUMDB=off go test -tags treedb_test -count=1 -p=1 -timeout=90s ./TreeDB/mvcc -run '^TestCommitAtPrimaryOnlyRetainsActualDataGeneration$'` passed with an actual run, no skip. This public activation check is additional to the default hosted matrix.\n- CI inventory refresh/check and its four maintenance/contract suites passed. Linux/macOS/Windows normal, Linux race, format/fault/reopen, M4, raw-path and existing performance workflows are running against this candidate; old PR-head results do not qualify it.\n\nBounded public performance evidence uses quiet host `192.168.0.111`, pinned Go1.26.3, CPU0/GOMAXPROCS1, prebuilt binaries and three balanced AB/BA/AB pairs. All samples are retained. These short comparisons establish direction and repair stability; they do not pass the final sprint targets.\n\n| Comparison | Before \u2192 after ns/op | Before \u2192 after ops/s | B/op | allocs/op |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Shared-slot/routing component: PRIMARY after DATA, 128 operations | 525,691 \u2192 501,221 | 1,902 \u2192 1,995 | 386,907 \u2192 368,446 | 535 \u2192 475 |\n| Subsequent ordinary cleanup repair: BatchWrite, 1,000 operations | 22,020 \u2192 22,074 | 45,413 \u2192 45,302 | 34,050 \u2192 34,050 | 132 \u2192 132 |\n| Same cleanup repair: PRIMARY after DATA, 128 operations | 502,864 \u2192 502,871 | 1,989 \u2192 1,989 | 368,448 \u2192 368,445 | 475 \u2192 475 |\n\nThe first comparison binds baseline `2a46465e` and the frozen 40-file component in the [source/raw/command packet](https://github.com/snissn/gomap/tree/4531e816968f89a10080164629c341d6c43e4f78/artifacts/4871/20261015-shared-custody-public-guard); it combines routing and custody effects. The repair comparison binds committed `fb8b23a3` versus the four-file ordinary-close repair with identical updated tests. PRIMARY generation advances remained zero in both repair arms. The final three-file packed-close fix runs outside these timers; its lifecycle evidence is separate. Setup, periodic checkpoint and DB teardown are excluded; batch Close is included. No percentages from these different comparisons are added together.\n\nRemaining merge gates: the complete nineteen-group ownership/caller matrix, actual platform/race and format/fault results, physical shrink/output and retained-memory costs, applicable matched performance guards, current-head independent review and green required CI. M4's public online route enforces at least 40% shrink and calls the unchanged 8\u00d7 production output guard; this is not a claim of a dedicated forced-overflow rejection test. Exhaustive graph/Dgraph closeout remains #4879.\n\n[Current execution state](https://github.com/snissn/gomap/issues/4871#issuecomment-6157916554) \u00b7 [Source-bound qualification progress](https://github.com/snissn/gomap/issues/4871#issuecomment-6191434279) \u00b7 [Native diagnostic decision](https://github.com/snissn/gomap/issues/4878#issuecomment-6191433730)\n",
